** Context :BLUEPRINT_BODY:
- This vault's Emacs config lives under
  universe/.../text-editors/emacs/Manifolding-Emacs/ and boots from
  ~/.config/emacs/init.el (static seed). Generated .el artifacts live
  ONLY in ~/.config/emacs/ (early-init.el, foundation-init.el,
  manifolding-emacs.el) — never write .el into the vault, except
  body-unfoldings/files/atlas.el which is a doct template SOURCE.
- Vault root self-discovers via .git/ marker. HOME is
  /data/data/com.termux/files/home (never /root). Real user files use
  real paths: no symlinks, no env vars for locations.
- WIP-DONT-TOUCH/ is forbidden: never read it for content, never write
  it, never reference it in code. Only exceptions in scope are .git/
  (skipped) and admin/ (live DB + admin notes, skipped by loader).

** Conventions :BLUEPRINT_BODY:
- All vault files are extensionless org. No .org suffix anywhere.
- Every loadable file: first headline carries :EMACS_MECHANISM:, with a
  :PROPERTIES: drawer holding :ID: plus :MM_PARENT: (note-id or none)
  and :MM_ORDER: (float). Files without mm keys are chainless: they
  load after the chain, alphabetically, with no error.
- Blueprint files: level-1 KEY headings carry :BLUEPRINT: merged into
  ONE contiguous colon run (spaces break the parser KEY match).
  Option lines carry :BLUEPRINT_BODY:. Unknown tags are ignored by the
  prompt parser; option text must have the body tag stripped on read.
- Templates: BODY_<NAME> :BLUEPRINT: KEY headings with no kind tag go
  to the template registry (never the prompt registry). Display names
  strip BODY_, downcase, _ to -.
- Never hardcode directory paths in code. Discover by tag scan
  (:EMACS_MECHANISM:, :BLUEPRINT:) or derive from an already-known
  file variable. yasnippet has no snippets dir (none exist on disk).

** Procedures :BLUEPRINT_BODY:
- New mechanism file: SPC v D (local) or SPC v L (module, prompts for
  :PACKAGE:/:STRAIGHT:/:CATEGORY:, writes headline props + leaf
  skeleton). New agent file: SPC v Q. New blueprint: SPC v P (born
  extensionless, pre-tagged KEY + ID + one tagged option).
- New files are born with :ID: drawers; placement afterward is manual
  via mm/assign-parent (writes back to the file drawer).
- Verification without booting: reader sweep of the tangled loader
  must be fully clean; per-file extraction
  (manifolding-emacs-concatenate-source-blocks) must report zero
  errors; tag/mm cross-counts must match disk exactly.
- Full boot is slow (>8 min) and runs only on explicit order. Never
  run it unasked.
